%N A398623 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} AH(k) * H(2*k) / k^2, where AH(k) = A058313(k)/A058312(k) is the k-th alternating harmonic (or skew-harmonic) number, and H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number.
%H A398623 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.57, p. 454, eq. (4.188), section 5.57, p. 469, section 6.57, pp. 794-798.
%H A398623 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398623 Equals 507*zeta(4)/64 - 7*log(2)*zeta(3)/4 + 5*log(2)^2*zeta(2)/4 - 7*log(2)^4/48 - 2*Pi*Im(Li_3((1+i)/2)) - 7*Li_4(1/2)/2, where i is the imaginary unit.
%e A398623 2.677075005516368529497490587614745464314576349590969...
%t A398623 RealDigits[507*Zeta[4]/64 - 7*Log[2]*Zeta[3]/4 + 5*Log[2]^2*Zeta[2]/4 - 7*Log[2]^4/48 - 2*Pi*Im[PolyLog[3, (1 + I)/2]] - 7*PolyLog[4, 1/2]/2, 10, 120][[1]]
